CAT = "ieqfaCpc"; SEG = "CPC"
Q = [
("The Consumer Protection Code 2025 applies to regulated firms from:",
 "24 March 2026", ["1 January 2025", "24 March 2025", "1 January 2027"],
 "The revised Code was published on 24 March 2025 and took effect on 24 March 2026, after a 12-month implementation period. The 2012 Code applied until then."),
("Which Standard for Business was added in the 2025 Code and heads the list?",
 "Secure customers' interests", ["Maximise shareholder returns", "Offer the lowest price", "Sell only Irish-made products"],
 "The Standards for Business Regulations 2025 open with the duty to secure customers' interests, alongside honesty and integrity, due skill, care and diligence, and acting in customers' best interests."),
("Under the Standards for Business, information a firm gives customers must be presented in a way that:",
 "Informs the customer effectively", ["Uses only the firm's own legal wording", "Fits on one side of a page", "Is read aloud to every customer"],
 "One of the Standards for Business is that all information provided to customers is presented in a way that informs them effectively."),
("Before recommending a financial service, the Code requires a firm to gather information on the consumer's needs and objectives, personal circumstances, financial situation and, where relevant:",
 "Risk attitude and sustainability wishes", ["Political views and religious beliefs", "Neighbours' income and their savings", "Preferred bank branch and its opening hours"],
 "The knowing the consumer rules list needs and objectives, personal circumstances, financial situation, attitude to risk and any sustainability preferences, as relevant to the service."),
("When gathering a consumer's attitude to risk, the Code says the firm must in particular find out:",
 "How important capital security is", ["How often they travel abroad on holiday", "Which newspaper they read", "How their parents invested"],
 "Regulation 16 says attitude to risk information includes, in particular, the importance of capital security to the consumer."),
("Before providing or arranging a financial service, a firm must give the consumer a statement of suitability that is:",
 "Signed, dated and on a durable medium", ["Given orally at the first fact-find meeting", "Sent only if the consumer asks", "Filed with the Central Bank first"],
 "The firm must prepare, sign and date a statement of suitability on paper or another durable medium, setting out why the service or product is considered suitable."),
("Which situation can exempt a firm from the knowing the consumer and suitability rules?",
 "Consumer picked product and provider alone", ["Consumer is in a hurry to buy cover today", "Adviser has known the consumer for years", "Product is sold only through the firm's website"],
 "Where the consumer instructs the firm to proceed with a product and provider they chose without any assistance, the suitability requirements do not apply. A term deposit under a year or a notice account is another exemption."),
("Before arranging a further financial service for an existing customer, a firm must:",
 "Check for material changes in their details", ["Repeat the first fact-find", "Charge a fee for updating its records", "Ask the Central Bank to approve the sale"],
 "Before a further service, the firm must seek confirmation of any material changes to the information it already holds and gather any extra information needed."),
("The Code defines a consumer in vulnerable circumstances as a natural person whose personal circumstances:",
 "Make them especially open to harm", ["Have lasted for more than two years", "Are recorded on a GP's medical certificate", "Mean they earn below a set income"],
 "Vulnerability may be permanent or temporary; what matters is that the person is especially susceptible to harm, particularly where a firm does not take appropriate care."),
("Once a firm has identified that a consumer is in vulnerable circumstances, it must:",
 "Give reasonable help as needed", ["Refuse to deal with them at all", "Refer them to the Central Bank", "Require a relative to sign for them"],
 "The firm must provide reasonable assistance to help the consumer deal with it, and must train consumer-facing staff to recognise and respond to vulnerability."),
("When a consumer buys through a firm's digital platform, the Code prohibits:",
 "Pre-ticked boxes saying terms were read", ["Online application forms", "Sending documents by email at all", "Offering a phone number for help"],
 "Firms must not provide preselected options indicating that the consumer has read or understood information. Consumers must also get clear step-by-step guidance on the platform."),
("Under the Code's digitalisation rules, algorithms used on a firm's digital platform must be:",
 "Documented and tested for fair outcomes", ["Hidden from all staff to prevent any misuse", "Approved in advance by the CCPC", "Changed every month for each user"],
 "Computer programs or algorithms must be designed to produce objective and consistent outcomes for consumers, properly documented and tested."),
("A warning statement required by the Code must appear:",
 "Boxed, bold and at least body text size", ["In small print at the very end of the document", "Only in the firm's terms of business", "On a separate page the consumer may skip"],
 "Warning statements must be prominent: in a box, in bold type and in a font size at least equal to the predominant font size of the document or advert."),
("A technical term that cannot be avoided in information for consumers must be:",
 "Explained in plain language", ["Printed in capital letters", "Repeated in every paragraph", "Printed in Irish too"],
 "The Code requires unavoidable technical terms to be explained in plain language where first used, or in a clearly referenced glossary."),
("A firm that plans to change the range of regulated services it offers must give affected consumers notice of at least:",
 "One month", ["One week", "Ten working days", "Six months"],
 "The firm must give clear notice on paper or another durable medium at least one month before the change, with enough detail to compare the position before and after."),
("A regulated firm that also offers unregulated services must keep its website information on regulated activities:",
 "On a separate webpage", ["Behind a customer login", "In a downloadable file only", "On a different firm's website"],
 "Regulated and unregulated activities must be on separate webpages, and written communications about unregulated activities carry a warning that they are not covered by Central Bank rules or a statutory compensation scheme."),
("An advert quotes research showing that customers prefer the firm. Under the Code, the advert must:",
 "Cite the research source and date", ["Remove the claim from every version", "Show the full research report on screen", "Get each customer's written consent"],
 "Research, statistics or claims in an advert must be substantiated, with the source, the date and any assumptions referred to in the advert."),
("Under the Code, the information in a firm's advertisements must be:",
 "Clear, fair, accurate, not misleading", ["Approved by the Central Bank in advance of use", "Limited to a single product per advert", "Written by an independent journalist"],
 "Design, presentation and content must be clear, fair, accurate and not misleading, and must not influence a consumer by ambiguity, exaggeration or omission."),
("A bank tells a customer a mortgage is available only if she also buys its home insurance. Under the Code this is:",
 "Prohibited contingent selling", ["Allowed if the price is fair", "Allowed for first-time buyers only", "A normal bundle of services"],
 "A firm must not make the sale of one financial service contingent on buying another from it or a connected party."),
("A firm may sell two products together as a bundle only where:",
 "There is an overall cost saving", ["Both products come from Ireland", "The consumer signs for both within a day", "One of the products is free"],
 "The Code bans bundling unless the firm can show an overall cost saving for the consumer, and it must show the cost of each product bought separately."),
("A consumer leaves a bundle but wants to keep one of its products. The firm must:",
 "Let her keep it, losing only the discount", ["Cancel both products on the same day", "Charge an exit fee equal to one year's premium", "Ask her to reapply as a new customer"],
 "When a consumer exits a bundle, she may keep any product she wishes without penalty or extra charge other than the loss of any discount."),
("Under the Code, a firm must resolve an error affecting consumers no later than:",
 "6 months after it was discovered", ["30 days after it was first discovered", "12 months after it occurred", "The next statutory audit"],
 "Errors must be resolved speedily and no later than six months after first discovery, including fixing the cause, refunding with appropriate interest and notifying affected consumers."),
("A firm cannot trace a former customer owed a refund after an error. Under the Code, the firm:",
 "Must not gain, and pays with interest if claimed", ["May keep the money after twelve months", "Must give the money to a registered charity at once", "Pays the refund to the Central Bank"],
 "If all reasonable steps fail, the firm must not benefit from the refund and must pay it with appropriate interest when the consumer claims it."),
("How often must a firm analyse the patterns and causes of errors affecting consumers?",
 "At least every 6 months", ["At least every 3 years", "Only after a complaint", "Only if asked"],
 "Error handling arrangements must include analysis of the rate, patterns and causes of errors at least once every six months."),
("Within how many working days must a firm acknowledge a written complaint on a durable medium?",
 "5", ["3", "10", "20"],
 "Regulation 105 requires acknowledgement within 5 working days, with details of the complaints procedure and, where relevant, the ombudsman."),
("While a complaint is being investigated, the firm must update the consumer at intervals of no more than:",
 "20 working days", ["5 working days", "40 working days", "3 calendar months"],
 "Updates on the progress of the investigation must be given on paper or another durable medium at intervals no greater than 20 working days from receipt."),
("A firm must try to resolve a complaint within 40 working days. If it cannot, it must:",
 "Give a likely timeframe and ombudsman details", ["Close the complaint file without issuing a decision", "Refund the consumer in full at once, with interest", "Report the consumer to the Central Bank"],
 "After 40 working days the firm must tell the consumer when it hopes to resolve the complaint and, where relevant, of their right to refer it to the ombudsman, with contact details."),
("Within how many working days of completing its investigation must a firm give the consumer its decision and reasons?",
 "5", ["2", "10", "15"],
 "The firm must advise the consumer on paper or another durable medium within 5 working days of completing the investigation, including any offer and the ombudsman's details."),
("A consumer complains by phone and the firm sorts it out to her satisfaction within two working days. Under the Code, the firm:",
 "May skip the full procedure but must log it", ["Must still send a final letter after 40 days", "Can treat it as never having happened", "Must report it to the ombudsman"],
 "The full procedure need not apply where a complaint is resolved to the consumer's satisfaction within 5 working days, but it must still be recorded in the complaints log."),
("Where the Code allows a firm to make an unsolicited call to a consumer, unless otherwise agreed in writing it may call only between:",
 "9 a.m. and 9 p.m., Monday to Saturday", ["8 a.m. and 10 p.m., on any day of the week", "9 a.m. and 5 p.m., Monday to Friday", "10 a.m. and 8 p.m., Monday to Sunday"],
 "Permitted calls may be made only between 9.00 a.m. and 9.00 p.m., Monday to Saturday, excluding public holidays, unless otherwise agreed in writing with the consumer."),
("At the start of a permitted sales call, the firm's representative must:",
 "Give their name and the call's purpose", ["Ask for the consumer's PPS number", "Confirm the consumer's current bank balance", "Offer a discount before going on"],
 "The representative must identify themselves and the firm, explain the purpose, say if the call is recorded and end the call at once if the consumer does not want it to continue."),
("For how long must a firm keep records of a consumer transaction after it is completed or discontinued?",
 "6 years", ["2 years", "10 years", "Until the customer dies"],
 "Regulation 117 requires records of consumer transactions to be kept for 6 years after the transaction is discontinued or completed."),
]
